"q-72099" :question/id #uuid "fdf680e3-0d0f-525f-8e37-64c868afcaa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-72099" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Consider a sphere such that its volume $V$ can vary. What is the best interpretation of ${r}^{′}(V)$ if $r$ is the length of the radius of the sphere?" :question/worked-solution "The function $r(V)$ gives the length of the radius of a sphere with volume $V.$ So,\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(V)=\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}V}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }r}{\\text{Change in }V}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${r}^{′}(V)$ is the rate at which the radius changes as the volume changes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-72099/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "159b4d58-b34d-52cd-aad2-2c058f772ad2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72099"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48684/selection/e6ce61b29f0ab3686822a32c3005e8bbabd5fcea8f76f4b885c3c4d70bb2593f" :answer/id #uuid "55d11992-046e-5370-b3a2-85e32fe92e62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the height changes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186063011 :answer-field/choices ["q-48684/selection/e6ce61b29f0ab3686822a32c3005e8bbabd5fcea8f76f4b885c3c4d70bb2593f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48684"] :question/worked-solution "The function $A(b)$ gives the area of a rectangle with base $b.$ So\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(b)=\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}b}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }A}{\\text{Change in }b}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${A}^{′}(b)$ is the rate at which the area changes as the base changes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-48686/selection/b753a83cc2afb01d2fc114a174414de9f08f385cf38ff8d2b238ca9b2780c3a6" :answer/id #uuid "c86889f3-39d8-527b-97ac-404d21630ad3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The length of each side of the square" :db/ensure 