ademy-id "q-48686" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Consider a square such that its area $A$ can vary. What is the best interpretation of ${s}^{′}(A)$ if $s$ is the length of each side of the square?" :question/worked-solution "The function $s(A)$ gives the length of each side of a square with area $A.$ So,\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(A)=\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}A}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }s}{\\text{Change in }A}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${s}^{′}(A)$ is the rate at which each side changes as the area changes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-48686/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "159b4d58-b34d-52cd-aad2-2c058f772ad2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72104/selection/351330c3b4c59f5c2f34ee720a44223d910f62492b98cdbb1df5d2eae37a1b10" :answer/id #uuid "5922755b-1461-5a2f-b42d-c95d924e22c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as each side changes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72104/selection/cc938a4c2ea75315855ad5968366992f9b0490610cd39c09ba75483e85d7284a" :answer/id #uuid "e6766686-6bb8-5c30-a317-cb6ed301ccfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The rate at which the perimeter changes as the area changes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72104/selection/04fb215a24f25b8ad79b7dbd1a8defedfde44ac696b341b757c8178db9b02b3a" :answer/id #uuid "a60668f8-0fa9-56d2-94b4-7aacdcb84ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The rate at which each side changes as the area changes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72104/selection/f87b53b6995c6d67adecb90979f2c508142fcc2b5cc4bf5a66098af37a8e0e62" :answer/id #uuid "107a582b-a0a1-5417-a6af-454af2c5f1eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The rate at which each side changes as the perimeter changes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72104/selection/29b125dfe7c5eff1aca9c1602b282f848650a3d