bd40e54eff5ad7848a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48691" :question/id #uuid "8ab35a06-9856-5b30-a012-87953b9c2934" :question/math-academy-id "q-48691" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The function $P(v)$ models the price of lemonade sold at a lemonade stand, in dollars, depending on the volume $v$ sold the previous day, in liters. What is the best interpretation of the statement below?\n\n$\\,$ *The slope of the tangent line to the graph of $P(v)$ at $v=4$ is equal to $0.5.$*" :question/worked-solution "The slope of the line tangent to the graph of $P(v)$ at $v=4$ gives the derivative of $P(v)$ at $v=4.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(4)=0.5.\n$$\n\nWe can interpret the above statement as\n\n$\\,$ *When $4$ liters of lemonade are sold the previous day, the price is increasing at a rate of $50$ cents per liter.*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48691/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2451a654-2255-5867-871d-54340dfeff81"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48571/selection/4319aa7fa22023b8a8090525605fec61278aa7438234fb5ef0e4ac7fa79d5970" :answer/id #uuid "81eea91d-8381-50e4-b2c5-9f8ccded11c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users decreased at a rate of $650$ users per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186062975 :answer-field/choices ["q-48571/selection/4319aa7fa22023b8a8090525605fec61278aa7438234fb5ef0e4ac7fa79d5970"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48571"] :question/worked-solution "The function ${U}^{′}(t)$ represents the rate at which the number of users is changing at the moment $t$ hours after launch. \n\nTherefore, ${U}^{′}(4)=650$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users increased at a rate of $650$ users per hour*" :question/difficulty :questio